# NPC standee lock (Tomas bevel v19)

Canonical construction: `assets/npcs/tomas_standee_bevel_v19.png` (option 3 routed wood-sign).

Every **current and future** generated character uses this exact physical design. Change clothes, face, pose, and name only.

**Must match Tomas:**
- Painted figure on a **chunky routed oak board** that follows the silhouette
- Visible **wood-grain edge / bevel** (highlight top-left, darker grain bottom-right)
- **Rectangular stained-wood foot**, not a circular cobblestone pedestal
- **One wood plaque** on the foot: four small corner rivets, name once in **black serif ALL-CAPS** (TOMAS, NESSA, BRAM, ELIRA)
- Isolated sprite; production shots use **lime green `#00FF00` chroma**, then knock out alpha
- No blue/gold HUD nameplate, compass badge, extra diorama base, or doubled lettering
- In-game: hide HTML nameplates; the plaque on the art is the name

**Do not** invent a new outline, cardboard halo, paper-doll tab, or stone plinth unless Marc unlocks this.

**Next session:** make Nessa, Bram, and Elira **background outlines** match Tomas v19 (same routed oak lip/bevel). Placement and Mark spots are done.

**In-game placement:** each location has four standing anchors with their own size (foreground larger, back smaller). Do not shrink every standee when more people are present. Place every new screen with the **Mark spots** tool (see `location-anchor-tool.mdc`).
